### ==============================================================================
### DecisionHub Backend API Test Suite
### Compatible with VS Code REST Client extension (humao.rest-client)
### ==============================================================================

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@contentType = application/json

### ==============================================================================
### 1. HEALTH CHECKS & SYSTEM STATUS
### ==============================================================================

### 1.1 Root Health Check
GET {{baseUrl}}/ HTTP/1.1

### 1.2 Health Check (v1 API)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/health HTTP/1.1

### 1.3 Health Check (Legacy Path)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/health HTTP/1.1



### ==============================================================================
### 2. AUTHENTICATION & USER MANAGEMENT
### ==============================================================================

### 2.1 Register New User - Success
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/register HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "fullName": "Alice Johnson",
  "email": "alice@example.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### 2.2 Register User - Duplicate Email (Expected: 400 Bad Request)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/register HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "fullName": "Alice Duplicate",
  "email": "alice@example.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### 2.3 Register User - Validation Error (Invalid Email & Short Password)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/register HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "fullName": "",
  "email": "not-an-email",
  "password": "short"
}

### 2.4 Login User - Success (Captures JWT token for subsequent requests)
# @name loginUser
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "alice@example.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### Store the JWT token from login response
@authToken = {{loginUser.response.body.token}}

### 2.5 Login User - Incorrect Password (Expected: 401 Unauthorized)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "alice@example.com",
  "password": "WrongPassword!"
}

### 2.6 Login User - Unknown Email (Expected: 401 Unauthorized)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "nonexistent.user@example.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}


### ==============================================================================
### 3. PROTECTED ENDPOINTS & AUTHORIZATION CHECKS
### ==============================================================================

### 3.1 Protected Endpoint Without Token (Expected: 401 Unauthorized)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/decisions HTTP/1.1

### 3.2 Protected Endpoint With Invalid Token (Expected: 401 Unauthorized)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/decisions HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer invalid-or-tampered-token-12345

### 3.3 Protected Endpoint With Valid Bearer Token (Passes Security Filter)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/decisions HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}


### ==============================================================================
### 4. SETUP DECISIONS FOR DISCUSSION TESTING
### ==============================================================================

### 4.1 Create Public Decision
# @name createPublicDecision
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/decisions HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

{
  "title": "Adopt Event-Driven Architecture",
  "description": "Discussion on adopting Apache Kafka for asynchronous communication.",
  "category": "Architecture",
  "visibility": "PUBLIC",
  "pollType": "SINGLE_CHOICE",
  "options": [
    { "title": "Kafka", "description": "High-throughput event streaming" },
    { "title": "RabbitMQ", "description": "Flexible AMQP routing" }
  ]
}

### Store Decision ID
@decisionId = {{createPublicDecision.response.body.data.id}}

### 4.2 Create Private Decision (For Access Control Tests)
# @name createPrivateDecision
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/decisions HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

{
  "title": "Confidential Executive Strategy",
  "description": "Internal restructuring and resource reallocation discussion.",
  "category": "Management",
  "visibility": "PRIVATE",
  "pollType": "SINGLE_CHOICE",
  "options": [
    { "title": "Option A", "description": "Internal realignment" },
    { "title": "Option B", "description": "External hiring" }
  ]
}

### Store Private Decision ID
@privateDecisionId = {{createPrivateDecision.response.body.data.id}}


### ==============================================================================
### 5. DISCUSSION MANAGEMENT (MILESTONE 3 - PHASE 1)
### ==============================================================================

### 5.1 Create Top-Level Comment on Decision
# @name createComment
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/decisions/{{decisionId}}/comments HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

{
  "content": "Kafka offers superior event persistence and partition scalability compared to traditional message brokers."
}

### Store Comment ID
@commentId = {{createComment.response.body.data.id}}

### 5.2 Create Second Comment on Decision
# @name createSecondComment
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/decisions/{{decisionId}}/comments HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

{
  "content": "We must also consider operational complexity and ZooKeeper/KRaft quorum management."
}

### 5.3 Retrieve Comments for Decision (Paginated, Chronological)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/decisions/{{decisionId}}/comments?page=0&size=10&sortBy=createdAt&sortDir=asc HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### 5.4 Update Own Comment
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/comments/{{commentId}} HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

{
  "content": "Kafka offers superior event persistence, partition scalability, and strict ordering guarantees per partition."
}

### 5.5 Reply to a Comment (Threaded Discussion)
# @name createReply
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/comments/{{commentId}}/replies HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

{
  "content": "Agreed, and consumer groups simplify horizontal scaling of worker microservices."
}

### Store Reply ID
@replyId = {{createReply.response.body.data.id}}

### 5.6 Retrieve Threaded Replies for Parent Comment (Paginated)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/comments/{{commentId}}/replies?page=0&size=10&sortBy=createdAt&sortDir=asc HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### 5.7 Retrieve Discussion Summary for Decision
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/decisions/{{decisionId}}/discussions/summary HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### 5.8 Register Second User (Bob) for Authorization Testing
# @name registerBob
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/register HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "fullName": "Bob Miller",
  "email": "bob@example.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### 5.9 Login Second User (Bob)
# @name loginBob
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "bob@example.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### Store Bob's Token
@bobToken = {{loginBob.response.body.token}}

### 5.10 Attempt Unauthorized Comment Modification (Bob edits Alice's comment - Expected: 403 Forbidden)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/comments/{{commentId}} HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{bobToken}}

{
  "content": "Hacked content: Bob attempting to modify Alice's comment."
}

### 5.11 Attempt to Comment on Private Decision Without Permission (Expected: 403 Forbidden)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/decisions/{{privateDecisionId}}/comments HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{bobToken}}

{
  "content": "Bob attempting to access and comment on a private executive decision."
}

### 5.12 Delete Own Comment (Soft Deletion - Preserves Child Replies)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/comments/{{commentId}} HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### 5.13 Verify Soft Deletion Preserves Threaded Discussion
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/decisions/{{decisionId}}/comments HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}


